diff --git a/ARCHITECTURE.md b/ARCHITECTURE.md
index 40f0cea..16a1ec0 100644
--- a/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -418,3 +418,30 @@ Regression coverage includes 24x8 dialogs, 40x12 diff focus switching, large
 review queues, long errors, empty searches, stale-target prevention, CI scrolling
 and resource-specific refresh recovery. No server writes are required for this
 polish verification.
+
+### Visual polish: conversation variant A
+
+The current experiment uses rounded conversation cards, one shared frame per
+thread and an accent left edge for focus. Replies retain their individual
+selection marker. Author names use info color, paths use link color, open threads
+use warning color and resolved threads use success color. Backgrounds are unchanged.
+Overview has no extra timeline rail. Suggestions use a label and colored code
+rows inside the shared card rather than nested frames. Narrow cards omit the code
+preview, retaining the file location and full comment text. The sidebar appears
+at 88 content columns. Resolved diff threads retain their disclosure row.
+
+Design alternatives and preserved references live in `docs/ui-examples`.
+The original is commit `6edd115`; `reference/first-experiment.patch` preserves
+the first experiment relative to that original. Keep the original as a candidate
+for a smaller color-only adjustment if A feels less clear in daily use.
+
+Rules for subsequent visual reviews:
+- Put task content first and metadata second.
+- Use one frame per conversation; avoid nested decoration.
+- Use accent for focus and consistent semantic colors for status.
+- Preserve navigation and identifiable comment targets at narrow widths.
+- Compare populated, empty and long-content layouts before extending a style.
+
+Populated Overview snapshots cover 100, 80 and 40 columns. Selection and fold
+regressions protect interaction targets and expanded content. Other views still
+need a visual pass against these rules.
